<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/1st-century-bce">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Ilerda</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/49-bce">49 BCE</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/1st-century-bce">1st century BCE</a> · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caesars-civil-war">Caesar's Civil War</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lleida">Ilerda</a> was <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/julius-caesar">Julius Caesar</a>'s campaign of June to August 49 BCE near modern Lleida in north-eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a> against the Pompeian <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/legatus">legates</a> Afranius and Petreius, at the start of his civil war. By manoeuvre and by cutting off their supplies rather than in a pitched battle, Caesar forced their surrender and secured Spain.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-ilerda.jpg" alt="Battle of Ilerda" width="320" height="427" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Theodore Ayrault Dodge · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Battle_of_Illerda,_map_1_(Caesar%CB%90_A_History_Of_The_Art_Of_War_Among_The_Romans_Down_To_The_End,_vol._II,_1892).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
